WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.610
- The thing with cooking
with color is that

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.080
by the end of this video,

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.600
my hands are going to be rainbow-colored.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.860
Hey, everyone, it's Inga.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.860
As many of you know, I love animation.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.630
I especially love Pixar movies.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:16.320
I also love making dishes
inspired by different colors.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.490
And today,

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.400
I'm gonna be doing something
a little bit different.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.160
I'll be picking five colors
from the color palette

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.650
of Pixar's "Turning Red," an attempt

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.960
to make a three-course meal

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.570
using only those five colors.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:31.770
Quick color palette breakdown.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.630
We have a burgundy red shade.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.600
We have a brighter vermilion shade of red,

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.180
then we have a rosy petal pastel pink,

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.250
and a lavender periwinkle.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.600
And then we have green.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.160
The reason I'm choosing "Turning Red"

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.440
is well, one, I love the movie.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.700
It's one of my favorites right now.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.280
I relate to the main
character, Meilin, so much.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.980
And two, I just think it
has such like a vibrant

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:56.190
and fun color palette that
is going to be challenging,

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.660
but exciting for us to work with.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.330
As you can see, these are
not the easiest colors

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:01.163
to work with

00:01:01.163 --> 00:01:05.370
because I'm trying to use only
natural-colored ingredients,

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.080
but we're gonna try and do it.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.676
So let's get started.

00:01:08.676 --> 00:01:11.310
(instrumental music)

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:14.010
To begin with, I want a lot of red,

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.460
and for this first dish,
I'm thinking red dumplings.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.620
It's just gonna be this super vibrant red

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:20.580
on the outside.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.810
And to get that red,

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.420
I'm going to use this
beet powder right here.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.230
I actually used it to make
pancakes in my 24-hour series.

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:29.640
I'm gonna make some beet water right now

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.010
just by adding the beet powder over here.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.750
I'm gonna add in some hot water

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.640
which will help this dissolve.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.910
Right in here, I'm going
to add in my flour slowly.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.020
I'm just gonna go in with my hands

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.910
because this is how I make it at home.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.260
I have my own family recipe.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:46.260
My grandpa made this
for me a lot as a kid,

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:48.510
just felt really appropriate
to do this today.

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:49.857
This is now formed into a dough.

00:01:49.857 --> 00:01:52.170
I'm just gonna sprinkle my counter here.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.200
Red is actually a really important
color in Chinese culture.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.790
It represents so many things

00:01:56.790 --> 00:02:00.330
like joy, luck, happiness,
just good fortune.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:02.370
And I think that's part of the reason

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:03.480
it's like the main color,

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.430
it's literally called "Turning Red."

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.590
I've been kneading this for quite a while.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:08.640
And look at this hand,

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.040
this is the power of beet, everybody.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.110
So now what I'm gonna do
is actually let this rest

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.630
for a little bit for
around half an hour or so.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:17.730
We'll be right back after this has rested.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:21.300
All right, we're back with
a rested dumpling dough.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.680
And this is what my grandpa taught me.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.750
I'm gonna roll it out into a log.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.240
And then we're going to section
it off into little pieces

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.310
before we roll them out into wrappers.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:31.020
I'm gonna cut these little bits out now.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.760
I cannot tell you the amount of times

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.350
I've watched my grandpa make this.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:35.183
This is what he does,

00:02:35.183 --> 00:02:36.660
and he does it like so much faster

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:37.860
than I'm doing it right now.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.260
We're just slowly rolling
out the edges here.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.730
You wanna thin out the edges

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.890
because that's the part
that's gonna fold together,

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.260
but you don't want it to
be so thin that it breaks.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:49.440
So this is the first wrapper,
it's around this big.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.600
I'm gonna continue making
some more right now.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.520
So I'm going to keep doing this

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:57.300
and we'll be back when I finish all of it.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.880
All right, we have our
dumpling wrappers rolled out.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.860
We're gonna go ahead and take one now.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.350
And I actually already
have some filling here.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.930
This is a dumpling filling
that I grew up having.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.370
It's my grandpa's recipe.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.530
Grandpa passed to mom, passed to me.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.170
I have a video on this, so
you can go check that out.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.010
We're gonna go ahead

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:16.890
and just scoop this into
our dumpling wrapper here.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:19.230
I always end up being too greedy here.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:23.040
I'm going to just put some
water around the edges

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.010
and then just fold it in like so.

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.270
It's like pleating it.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:30.300
And you see, the beautiful
thing about homemade wrappers is

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:34.140
that it really just does
stick together so easily.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:37.470
And there you have a beautiful
little beet dumpling.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:40.500
Green in the movie, I feel
like kinda represents the mom.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.420
Mei's room is also green,

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:44.730
where she's this super vibrant red.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:45.960
So it's almost like she's trying

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:48.600
to break out of this system that she's in,

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.240
like how I think her mom wants to be calm

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:54.060
and collected, and she's
like, "But I am emotions!"

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:55.260
So the red and green I think

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.090
is a very interesting contrast there

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.380
between her and her mom.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.270
My mom and I actually
make dumplings together.

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:02.730
By the time I make one,
she's already made like five.

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:04.710
So let me finish up here

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.720
and then we can bring the steamer in

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:07.830
and get these going.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:08.663
I'm back.

00:04:08.663 --> 00:04:11.100
I have my beautiful bamboo steamer here.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.480
It's huge.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.020
So normally, I would actually
steam with parchment paper

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.910
or if I have some sort of steaming cloth

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:18.743
with me at home.

00:04:18.743 --> 00:04:21.360
But today, to fit the
theme of red and green,

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.040
I'm gonna steam it over cabbage.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.660
All right, so this is looking good.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.800
Now I'm going to put my
dumplings right on top.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.780
I made like really big dumplings.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:33.360
I was really excited about the filling.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.940
So now I'm gonna put
these right over the pot,

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:36.773
closing in.

00:04:36.773 --> 00:04:38.490
This is gonna take a
couple of minutes to steam,

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.020
probably a little longer than expected

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.370
because I made them so big,

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:44.100
but I'm excited to see how these turn out.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:44.933
Woo-hoo!

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:49.020
Look at how beautiful that red is!

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:50.850
So I'm gonna plate this on here.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:53.610
And I also have some chives and chili oil.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:55.350
I think I'm just excited
because I'm hungry.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:56.610
Why did I make them so big?

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:57.570
What am I gonna do?

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:58.680
Can I fit them all?

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.270
Look at how big this is.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:01.103
Oh my God.

00:05:01.103 --> 00:05:01.936
Here you go.

00:05:01.936 --> 00:05:02.850
This is what it looks like.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:05.430
All right, I'm gonna put
some chili oil right in here.

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.290
And once again, to fit our color palette,

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:10.290
we're gonna add a sprinkle of
green in the form of chives.

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.830
So Meilin and her mother are one.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.090
And there you have it,

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:18.240
that is the first dish
of our three-course meal.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:19.800
But for now, we're gonna go ahead

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:22.380
and work on our second course.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:23.213
We're back.

00:05:23.213 --> 00:05:24.540
And I have moved on

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.210
to the main dish of our three-course meal,

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:28.830
it's called hong shao rou.

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:31.020
So the first step I'm doing here is just

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:34.530
melting some rock sugar in some hot oil.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:37.440
This is to help caramelize the pork belly

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.270
which we're going to add later.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:41.520
The pork belly here has
already been blanched

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.840
for a few minutes.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.790
This is looking kind of melted.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:47.940
You can see that the sugar
has now become little puddles

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:49.020
of golden brown.

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:51.240
So this is where I'm gonna
add in the pork belly.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.670
So I'm gonna let this
just sit for a little bit.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:55.950
What I thought was really
cool too, about "Turning Red"

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:58.170
and the foods featured
in it is that the team

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.670
and the art team specifically,

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:02.490
actually put a lot of
effort into doing research

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:04.080
for everything you see in the film.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.780
I was also talking to the
director, Domee Shi, briefly,

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:08.670
and she told me that most of the dishes

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:11.490
featured in the movie are a combination

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:13.980
of Taishanese and Cantonese cuisine.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.750
Another thing that I
forgot to bring up earlier

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.940
about the dumplings is
that the dumplings featured

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:20.370
in "Turning Red" are actually an homage

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:24.120
to her mom's background
from the north of China.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:26.370
It is a beautiful golden brown.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:29.430
I have both light soy
sauce and dark soy sauce.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:30.900
So adding both of those in,

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:33.450
and also some rice wine,

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.220
I believe this is Shaoxing rice wine.

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:37.260
Now I'm just going to add in the water,

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:38.580
and I know that's a lot of water,

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:39.960
but we're gonna be braising this.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.370
We're going to be cooking this down

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:43.200
around like 45 minutes or so.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.850
So I'm going to let this do its thing,

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:47.580
and we're gonna get started
working on our rice.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:50.160
So again, to stick with the color palette

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.430
that we have today, I'm thinking
we can make purple rice,

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:56.100
which I have done before,
I only ate purple foods

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:56.940
for 24 hours.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:58.290
To change it up a little bit,

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:00.990
and I'm actually going
to dye my white rice

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:03.120
and purple cabbage.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:05.070
What we have here is just
sliced purple cabbage

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.720
that we've boiled for 15 minutes,

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:09.180
and then steeped again for 15 minutes.

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:11.790
I'm gonna use this liquid to cook my rice.

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.800
So I'm gonna first strain this.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:16.080
I'm gonna go ahead and
put my rice in here first.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.790
And then we're just gonna fill this up.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.040
It looks like I put like
so much food dye in here,

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:23.250
but this is really, truly
just purple cabbage itself.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:24.270
Gonna let this rice cook.

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:25.830
I think pork belly's pretty much done,

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:27.240
and we can plate this up.

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:29.190
I have some cilantro here on my plate.

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:31.020
So now we're going to
plate up our pork belly.

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:33.090
So we're going to just place that on here.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:35.700
We're serving this up family
style, hence, the plating.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:36.870
That's why I'm plating everything in.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.060
I'm not eating this all
by myself, I promise.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.290
Or maybe I am, who knows?

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:42.720
I'm only going to put
one bowl of rice for now

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.880
just so you guys can
see what it looks like,

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:47.310
but this is my purple rice.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:48.143
Look at that.

00:07:48.143 --> 00:07:50.640
Here's our second course.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:52.920
We have one more course to go through.

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:53.753
Gonna be dessert.

00:07:53.753 --> 00:07:54.586
It's gonna be sweet.

00:07:54.586 --> 00:07:55.419
It's gonna be fantastic.

00:07:55.419 --> 00:07:56.400
So BRB.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:57.660
I'm thinking donuts.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.940
So remember that one breakfast scene

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:03.480
where Meilin's mom, Ming,
prepares the congee,

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:04.500
the breakfast porridge.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.560
And then she also has this
little box of donut holes.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:10.440
So there's like both Eastern
and Western food on a table

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.480
which is something I
feel like I grew up with.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:14.070
So fun fact, the donuts

00:08:14.070 --> 00:08:16.080
from their movie are
actually from Tim Hortons

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:18.300
and they actually have this
product called Timbits.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:21.330
So today, I'm going to make
something kind of like Timbits.

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:23.820
So even before I go into
making the donut holes,

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:26.790
I'm going to make some homemade sprinkles

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:28.470
because we really wanna be sure

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:30.090
to get those colors right.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:31.980
I'm gonna be making both purple

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:34.800
and green sprinkles with
different food colorings,

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:35.760
natural food colorings.

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:37.290
Purple, we're doing ube.

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:40.950
And then for green, we're
going with this pandan extract.

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:41.970
So we're gonna get started

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:44.220
by having some powdered sugar here,

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:45.600
and to this powdered sugar,

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:50.040
I am going to add in a tablespoon of water

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:52.800
and I'm going to put in corn syrup.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.680
The thing with cooking
with color too, is that

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.150
by the end of this video,

00:08:57.150 --> 00:08:59.670
my hands are going to be rainbow-colored.

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:01.140
So, oh!

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.550
Accidents happen, and that's okay.

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:05.760
I think we have roughly a
teaspoon of ube extract here.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:06.690
Ooh, okay, see.

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:09.690
I was afraid that I was
going to put too much,

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:13.080
but I feel like this
should be okay so far.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:14.280
So for those of you who are not familiar

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:17.160
with the flavor of ube,
it's kind of like vanilla,

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.900
but also like coconut-ish.

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:21.180
So here's what we have so far.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:23.880
I'm going to now put
this in the piping bag,

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:26.130
so then we can pipe out our sprinkles.

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:28.440
This is the part where you
need real steady hands.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:29.460
Okay, here we go.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:31.410
I'm gonna pipe these into straight lines

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:33.660
and then we're gonna have to break this up

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:34.890
into sprinkle form.

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:36.240
I think I'm pretty much finished

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:38.790
with my purple sprinkles here.

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:40.440
I'm going to now do the same thing

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:42.960
with my pandan extract, the green ones.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.640
And we're just gonna
fill the rest of this up.

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:47.730
We actually need to dry this
for around six hours or so.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.160
Luckily, I have an
incredible culinary team

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:51.960
who has already prepped some for me.

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:52.920
So I'm gonna swap these out.

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:54.990
And then we can go into
making the donut holes.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:57.660
Now to make the actual donut batter,

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:59.190
I'm gonna start with some flour,

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:03.060
and then baking powder, sugar, and salt.

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:04.530
Dry ingredients in one bowl,

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:06.810
and then wet ingredients
in the other bowl.

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:07.890
I have some milk here.

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:10.530
I'm gonna plop in my
egg yolks, one egg yolk.

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:12.570
Put in a little bit of vanilla extract.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:15.330
Whisk this really quickly together.

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:18.030
Now I'm just gonna
combine the two together

00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:19.770
until we have a batter.

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:22.350
I'm gonna go into adding
my melted butter here.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:26.130
And this batter is more of
like a clumpy thicker batter.

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:27.540
I think this looks pretty good.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:30.690
It is now a very sticky dough.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:31.830
So now that this is done,

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:34.290
I am going to start frying my donut holes.

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:36.360
Frying station is now ready and set up.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:38.040
So I have a little ice cream scoop here.

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:40.890
This is what I'm gonna use
to scoop out my donut batter.

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:41.820
Woo-hoo.

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:43.380
All right, it's in, it's in, it's in.

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:44.880
This just really helps make sure

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:47.070
that it's all evenly sized.

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:49.200
These don't have to be
in here for that long,

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:50.730
just around two minutes or so,

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:52.680
until they're a nice golden brown.

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:53.610
Okay!

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:56.910
These are now a beautiful brown,

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:58.320
so I'm gonna take them
out before they burn.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:10:59.340
So now I'm gonna go ahead

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:01.710
and finish frying up the rest of this.

00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:04.800
And then we can go into
decorating, making the glaze.

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:07.200
My donut holes are ready
and they've cooled down.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:10.440
Gonna set this here for now,
while I work on the glaze,

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.800
which we will make into
a light pastel pink,

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:16.740
which actually apparently,
the pastel pink colors

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:19.020
and purple were inspired by "Sailor Moon."

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:20.670
It's like very dreamy transformation.

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:23.640
The film is supposed to
be set in the early 2000s.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:25.830
So it's kind of like that boy band,

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.470
pop culture, fun tween energy.

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:30.720
So we're just going with
that kind of vibe here.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:33.180
Light pink is sort of the running theme

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:34.770
that we also see in "Turning Red."

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:36.300
You remember those like pink clouds

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:39.240
that kinda poof up when Mei
turns into the red panda?

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:41.010
It's kind of like a transformation thing.

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:42.270
It's very dreamy.

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:43.800
In order to try to make this light pink,

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.030
I am using a combination

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:47.550
of both strawberry powder and beet powder.

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:49.410
Give this a gentle toss

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:52.440
just to make sure all
the colors are in here.

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:55.170
And then now, I'm going to add in my milk.

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:57.630
When I was a teenager, of
course, I was into boy bands.

00:11:57.630 --> 00:11:59.910
I feel like everybody
goes through that phase.

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:02.550
Did I have posters on
my wall at one point?

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:04.080
No, because my mom wouldn't let me.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:07.893
But did I wanna go to a
concert and sneak out?

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:09.743
I didn't sneak out.

00:12:09.743 --> 00:12:11.460
I asked for permission. (chuckles)

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:12.600
Oh yeah, it looks really good.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.100
I'm gonna dip my donut holes in here

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:16.200
and then we're gonna sprinkle some purple

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:17.340
and green sprinkles on there.

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:18.180
Look at that.

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:19.140
Beautiful!

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:20.550
Before it dries up,

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:23.310
I'm going to quickly sprinkle some green

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:24.900
and purple sprinkles on here.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:26.370
All right, amazing!

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:27.990
I hope Tim Horton is proud.

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:31.920
Here we are, our final course
for our three-course meal,

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:34.440
these beautiful pink purple green donuts.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:36.150
I think it's time to
bring everything else in,

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:38.280
so you guys can have the full picture

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:40.530
of what this entire meal looks like.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:41.363
Okay!

00:12:41.363 --> 00:12:43.950
Here we have the whole
meal and all five colors,

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.900
burgundy red, vermilion red,

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:48.180
lavender periwinkle, pastel pink,

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:49.830
and emerald green.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:51.360
Playing with natural food coloring

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:53.850
can always be a little bit intimidating

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:55.350
and you never really know what to expect,

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:58.113
but I feel like the colors
really came through.

00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:00.900
Dumpling's obviously amazing.

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:03.300
Oh my God, homemade
wrappers are chewy and cute.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:04.980
And this sauce, oh my God.

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:06.060
Pork belly.

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:07.443
Look at how shiny it is.

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:11.340
Because it's been braised, it's so tender.

00:13:11.340 --> 00:13:12.640
And eat it with some rice.

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:16.830
Mm, this purple cabbage
hack is just incredible.

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:18.830
Last but not least, gotta try my donuts.

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:21.923
Very good.

00:13:21.923 --> 00:13:22.920
It's like freeze-dried strawberries.

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:23.753
Oh my gosh.

00:13:23.753 --> 00:13:24.990
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:25.980
I had so much fun.

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:27.330
If you have a movie you love

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:30.480
